1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Never turn your back on the past.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Seraphim Falls is a western, action, drama film directed by David Von Ancken.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
The Civil War has ended, but Colonel Morsman Carver is on one final
mission – to kill Gideon, no matter what it takes.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Launched by a gunshot and propelled by rage, the relentless pursuit takes the two men through frigid snow-capped mountains and
arid deserts, far from the comforts and codes of civilisation, into the bloodiest recesses of their own souls.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Carver, played by Liam Neeson.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Gideon, played by Pierce Brosnan.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Hayes, played by Michael Wincott.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Railroad Foreman, played by Xander Berkeley.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Parsons, played by Ed Lauter.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Henry, played by Kevin J. O'Connor.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Seraphim Falls is a 2006 American revisionist Western film directed by television
producer and director David Von Ancken in his only feature film.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
The storyline was conceived from a screenplay written
by Von Ancken and Abby Everett Jaques.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
The fictional story focuses on a bounty hunt for a Union soldier by a
Confederate colonel following the American Civil War in the late 1860s.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
Pierce Brosnan, Liam Neeson, Michael Wincott, Tom Noonan,
and Ed Lauter star in principal roles.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Seraphim Falls explores civil topics, such as violence, human survival and war.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
The film was produced by the motion picture studio of Icon Productions.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
It was commercially distributed by Samuel Goldwyn Films and Destination Films
theatrically, and by Sony Pictures Home Entertainment for home media.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film score was composed by musician Harry Gregson-Williams, although a
soundtrack version for the motion picture was not released to the public.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
Seraphim Falls premiered at the 2006 Toronto International Film Festival and was released to theatres in limited
release in the United States on January 26, 2007, grossing $418,296 in domestic ticket sales.

20
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
It earned an additional $801,762 in box office business overseas for
a combined worldwide total of $1,220,058 in revenue.

21
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
The film generally received positive critical reviews
before its initial screening in cinemas.

22
01:41:12,000 --> 01:41:18,000
Notable similarities have been found between the film and the 1976 revisionist
western, The Outlaw Josey Wales directed by Clint Eastwood.

23
01:45:48,000 --> 01:45:54,000
The film explores themes of colonel, frontier, stalking, storm, remedy.

24
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
The tone is emotional.
